{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 4958062,
  "courseSlug": "remix-course",
  "courseTitle": "Remix.js - The Practical Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "34674378",
      "title": "What Is Remix? And Why Would You Use Remix?",
      "lectureOrder": 2,
      "videoOrder": 2,
      "sourceHash": "71c8eb504236327215f0914fc802edd1a31cdf7d22c793b31c2a403e78dad789",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.1,
          "end": 5.07,
          "en": "So what is Remix?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.07,
          "end": 8.91,
          "en": "Well, it is a framework for ReactJS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.91,
          "end": 12.9,
          "en": "And that, of course, brings up one important question.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.9,
          "end": 16.83,
          "en": "Isn't ReactJS already a library?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 16.83,
          "end": 18.36,
          "en": "Yes, it of course is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.36,
          "end": 21.27,
          "en": "ReactJS is a JavaScript library",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.27,
          "end": 23.67,
          "en": "for building user interfaces,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.67,
          "end": 28.02,
          "en": "highly reactive user interfaces to be precise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.02,
          "end": 31.14,
          "en": "So why do we need Remix then?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.14,
          "end": 34.95,
          "en": "Well, Remix builds up on top of ReactJS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.95,
          "end": 37.83,
          "en": "so you will still write React code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.83,
          "end": 42.09,
          "en": "but Remix adds a lot of extra features that simplify",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 42.09,
          "end": 47.09,
          "en": "the process of building full-stack applications with React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 47.31,
          "end": 49.92,
          "en": "Because if you're using Just-React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 49.92,
          "end": 52.71,
          "en": "if you have a normal React project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 52.71,
          "end": 55.53,
          "en": "like I have it here in this frontend folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 55.53,
          "end": 57.24,
          "en": "then you have a lot of code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 57.24,
          "end": 60.06,
          "en": "that deals with displaying a user interface.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 60.06,
          "end": 63.36,
          "en": "However, if that application also needs a backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 63.36,
          "end": 66.6,
          "en": "where you, for example, store data in a database,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.6,
          "end": 69.93,
          "en": "you must add code to that React application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 69.93,
          "end": 74.91,
          "en": "that sends requests to that separate backend server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 74.91,
          "end": 77.07,
          "en": "which then runs some server-side code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 77.07,
          "end": 79.8,
          "en": "that does actually talk to the database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 79.8,
          "end": 82.2,
          "en": "So in your front-end React application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 82.2,
          "end": 85.14,
          "en": "you have code for sending requests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 85.14,
          "end": 87.6,
          "en": "for managing some loading state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 87.6,
          "end": 91.05,
          "en": "whilst the request is on its way so that you, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 91.05,
          "end": 95.78999999999999,
          "en": "can show some loading spinner or some loading display",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 95.78999999999999,
          "end": 98.22,
          "en": "and for handling any potential errors",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 98.22,
          "end": 99.69,
          "en": "that might be sent back.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 99.69,
          "end": 102.6,
          "en": "That's what you do on the front-end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 102.6,
          "end": 106.83,
          "en": "And as mentioned, what you need then is a separate backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 106.83,
          "end": 110.31,
          "en": "if you wanna build a full-stack application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 110.31,
          "end": 112.44,
          "en": "So that's a totally different project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 112.44,
          "end": 116.03999999999999,
          "en": "for example, built with node and ExpressJS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 116.03999999999999,
          "end": 119.46000000000001,
          "en": "but you could build it with any programming language.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 119.46000000000001,
          "end": 122.04,
          "en": "And there, you then do the actual work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 122.04,
          "end": 125.55,
          "en": "of reaching out to a database or to a file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 125.55,
          "end": 128.73,
          "en": "or wherever you're storing your data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 128.73,
          "end": 130.74,
          "en": "You could build such a backend yourself,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 130.74,
          "end": 134.1,
          "en": "or you're using some third party service like Firebase.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 134.1,
          "end": 137.37,
          "en": "But either way, you have a detached separate backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 137.37,
          "end": 140.55,
          "en": "That's how you normally build full-stack applications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 140.55,
          "end": 143.13,
          "en": "when using React for the front-end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 143.13,
          "end": 145.98,
          "en": "And it's really important to understand and keep in mind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 145.98,
          "end": 148.11,
          "en": "that in your front-end application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 148.11,
          "end": 150.32999999999998,
          "en": "in the React app you're building,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 150.32999999999998,
          "end": 153.3,
          "en": "you are not directly talking to some database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 153.3,
          "end": 154.71,
          "en": "or anything like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 154.71,
          "end": 157.953,
          "en": "Instead, you're sending requests to the separate backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 158.79,
          "end": 162.12,
          "en": "Now that request sending is often done with useEffect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 162.12,
          "end": 163.2,
          "en": "which wraps the code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 163.2,
          "end": 166.44,
          "en": "for sending such a fetch request for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 166.44,
          "end": 169.74,
          "en": "Or if you're using the latest version of React Router,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 169.74,
          "end": 173.55,
          "en": "you could also use the new API offered by React Router",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 173.55,
          "end": 177.15,
          "en": "for adding loaders and actions for sending requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 177.15,
          "end": 180.18,
          "en": "when a route becomes active, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 180.18,
          "end": 182.28,
          "en": "You still have a separate backend with that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 182.28,
          "end": 183.9,
          "en": "but the React code you have to write",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 183.9,
          "end": 186.09,
          "en": "gets much easier and leaner.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 186.09,
          "end": 189.33,
          "en": "But I do cover React Router in my full React course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 189.33,
          "end": 191.07,
          "en": "and also in a separate video,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 191.07,
          "end": 193.68,
          "en": "which I created for my YouTube channel.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 193.68,
          "end": 196.05,
          "en": "Either way, you have a detached backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 196.05,
          "end": 198.36,
          "en": "Now, if you are using Remix instead,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 198.36,
          "end": 201.75,
          "en": "and, of course, you'll learn how to create Remix projects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 201.75,
          "end": 205.41,
          "en": "and which features Remix offers throughout this course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 205.41,
          "end": 209.28,
          "en": "but if you're using Remix, then these things change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 209.28,
          "end": 212.04,
          "en": "You still build a React application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 212.04,
          "end": 214.05,
          "en": "you still have a React component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 214.05,
          "end": 215.85,
          "en": "you still write React code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 215.85,
          "end": 220.29,
          "en": "but you blend your server-side code into the same file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 220.29,
          "end": 222.78,
          "en": "where you define your components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 222.78,
          "end": 225.84,
          "en": "So you have a mixture of front-end and backend code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 225.84,
          "end": 227.22,
          "en": "in the same file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 227.22,
          "end": 228.99,
          "en": "The code here might look similar",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 228.99,
          "end": 231.24,
          "en": "to what you saw with React Router",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 231.24,
          "end": 232.82999999999998,
          "en": "since I also have such a loader",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 232.82999999999998,
          "end": 234.6,
          "en": "and such a action function here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 234.6,
          "end": 236.79,
          "en": "but here, we then actually have code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 236.79,
          "end": 240,
          "en": "that runs on the server, some backend code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 240,
          "end": 241.11,
          "en": "And therefore, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 241.11,
          "end": 243.45,
          "en": "building a full-stack React application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 243.45,
          "end": 246.33,
          "en": "becomes much easier because you have one project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 246.33,
          "end": 249.9,
          "en": "and backend and front-end code work together seamlessly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 249.9,
          "end": 254.37,
          "en": "And Remix, this framework, automatically splits your code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 254.37,
          "end": 258.09,
          "en": "such that only the front-end code is served to your users",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 258.09,
          "end": 260.58,
          "en": "so they never see your backend code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 260.58,
          "end": 263.85,
          "en": "which could also contain sensible data, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 263.85,
          "end": 265.53,
          "en": "And on the other hand, the backend code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 265.53,
          "end": 267.57,
          "en": "is executed on a server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 267.57,
          "end": 271.14,
          "en": "As a side effect that must not be underestimated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 271.14,
          "end": 275.25,
          "en": "the users of your website, so the visitors of your website,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 275.25,
          "end": 277.44,
          "en": "all they receive is the finished website",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 277.44,
          "end": 279.21,
          "en": "when visiting your website.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 279.21,
          "end": 282.42,
          "en": "So they get the finished HTML page with all the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 282.42,
          "end": 284.31,
          "en": "already injected into the page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 284.31,
          "end": 287.58,
          "en": "which also helps a lot with search engine optimization.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 287.58,
          "end": 291.06,
          "en": "Since those search engine crawlers see the full website,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 291.06,
          "end": 293.88,
          "en": "including all the data that makes up that website,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 293.88,
          "end": 296.76,
          "en": "instead of just seeing the empty skeleton",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 296.76,
          "end": 299.67,
          "en": "that is yet to be populated by React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 299.67,
          "end": 302.49,
          "en": "by the client side code that is yet to execute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 302.49,
          "end": 305.4,
          "en": "after the first version of the page has been loaded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 305.4,
          "end": 308.31,
          "en": "So that's a major advantage you get when using Remix",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 308.31,
          "end": 311.16,
          "en": "because Remix pre-renders all these components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 311.16,
          "end": 312.99,
          "en": "and all these pages on the server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 312.99,
          "end": 316.05,
          "en": "and then serves the finished page to your end users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 316.05,
          "end": 319.77,
          "en": "So that's what Remix is, and why you might wanna use it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 319.77,
          "end": 321.51,
          "en": "It simplifies the process",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 321.51,
          "end": 323.79,
          "en": "of building full-stack React application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 323.79,
          "end": 327.66,
          "en": "by merging the code bases and it gives you many advantages,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 327.66,
          "end": 330.39,
          "en": "and Remix has a couple of other amazing features.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 330.39,
          "end": 332.7,
          "en": "And to be honest, writing Remix code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 332.7,
          "end": 336,
          "en": "and building Remix apps simply is a lot of fun",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 336,
          "end": 338.073,
          "en": "because it's such an amazing framework.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
